From: PS5 Linux Kernel Team <kernel@ps5-linux.local>
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] mt7921e: add Salina PCIe initialization retry quirk and bus hang check

On PS5 models with Salina southbridge (CFI-12xx and Slim revisions),
reference clock stabilization may delay MCU responsiveness during
cold boot or kexec hand-off, triggering transient "driver own failed"
(-5 / LPCTL stuck at 0x4) errors.

Introduce bounded retry loop with usleep_range(2000, 5000) for driver
ownership acquisition. In addition, check for Salina bus hang (register
read 0xffffffff) to prevent cascading hardware panics.

Signed-off-by: PS5 Linux Kernel Team <kernel@ps5-linux.local>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/pci.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/pci.c
index 8e45b12..6c19a43 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/pci.c
@@ -404,9 +404,32 @@ static int mt7921_pci_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev,
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_free_dev;
 
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_X86_PS5)
+	/*
+	 * Salina Southbridge PCIe PHY clock initialization can delay MCU
+	 * readiness during cold boot or kexec. Add bounded retry loop before
+	 * asserting driver-own failure.
+	 */
+	for (int retry = 0; retry < 5; retry++) {
+		ret = __mt792xe_mcu_drv_pmctrl(dev);
+		if (!ret)
+			break;
+		usleep_range(2000, 5000);
+	}
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_free_dev;
+
+	chipid = mt7921_l1_rr(dev, MT_HW_CHIPID);
+	if (chipid == 0xffffffff) {
+		dev_err(mdev->dev, "Salina PCIe bus hang detected (chipid 0xffffffff)\n");
+		ret = -ENODEV;
+		goto err_free_dev;
+	}
+#else
 	ret = __mt792xe_mcu_drv_pmctrl(dev);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_free_dev;
 
 	chipid = mt7921_l1_rr(dev, MT_HW_CHIPID);
+#endif
 	if (chipid == 0x7961 && (mt7921_l1_rr(dev, MT_HW_BOUND) & BIT(7)))
-- 
